<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deioces</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 678–c. 655 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Deioces was the traditional founder of the Median kingdom (r. c. 678–c. 655 BCE), known chiefly from the account of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>. He is credited with uniting the Median tribes and establishing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecbatana">Ecbatana</a> as their capital. His historicity and the details of his reign remain debated, but he stands at the beginning of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/median-empire">Median Empire</a>'s story.</p></div>
